# --- accelerometer / movement ----------------------------------------------

config APP_ACC_MOVEMENT_THRESHOLD
	int "Movement delta threshold (milli-g)"
	default 150

config APP_MOVEMENT_CONFIRM_MS
	int "Movement confirmation window (ms)"
	default 10000

config APP_MOVEMENT_CONFIRM_HITS
	int "Required above-threshold samples to confirm"
	default 6
	help
	  accel_confirm_movement() polls every 100 ms for
	  APP_MOVEMENT_CONFIRM_MS, so the window offers
	  APP_MOVEMENT_CONFIRM_MS/100 polls and this must stay comfortably
	  below that number — set equal to it and every single sample has to
	  clear the threshold, which real movement never manages because
	  changes of direction pass through ~1 g.  A BUILD_ASSERT in
	  hw_accel.c rejects that case outright.

	  6 is 600 ms of cumulative motion, which a hand pushing the unit
	  around clears easily while a single knock does not.  Hits
	  accumulate over the whole window and need not be consecutive.

config APP_MOVEMENT_INACTIVITY_RESET
	int "Inactivity reset timer (seconds)"
	default 1800

config APP_MOVEMENT_ALARM
	bool "Enable movement alarm"
	default n

config APP_CRASH_THRESHOLD_MG
	int "Impact alert threshold (milli-g)"
	default 4000
	help
	  Acceleration delta that triggers an impact alert while awake.
	  Production ~4000 (4 g); set ~1200 in local.conf for bench testing —
	  a firm rap on the desk reaches 1.5-3 g.  Rounded down to 125 mg
	  steps (±8 g FS / 64).

config APP_IMPACT_IMMEDIATE_MG
	int "Report an impact without waiting for the movement confirm (milli-g, 0 = never)"
	default 700
	help
	  Peak | |a| - 1g | from the FIFO ring, drained the moment an accel
	  wake arrives, that is reported straight away instead of after
	  accel_confirm_movement() has spent up to APP_MOVEMENT_CONFIRM_MS
	  deciding whether the unit is being moved.  The confirm still runs
	  afterwards, so a hit followed by movement raises both alerts.

	  Must sit above APP_PARKED_IMPACT_MG and below the clip ceiling:
	  sleep runs the accel at +/-2 g, so the deviation saturates around
	  1000-1200 mg and a threshold above that can never fire.  That
	  leaves a narrow window, which is why APP_IMPACT_IMMEDIATE_MAX_MS
	  qualifies it by duration as well.  Set 0 to disable and always
	  wait for the confirm.

config APP_IMPACT_IMMEDIATE_MAX_MS
	int "Longest event still treated as an impact (ms)"
	default 300
	help
	  Amplitude alone cannot separate a hit from someone taking firm hold
	  of the unit, because both clip at +/-2 g.  Duration can: an impact
	  is a spike of tens of ms, while movement stays above the noise for
	  hundreds.  An over-threshold wake lasting longer than this is left
	  to the movement confirm instead of being reported as an impact.
	  Measured as accel_impact.over_ms — time with the deviation above
	  250 mg — which the ring resolves in 38 ms steps (26 Hz batching).

config APP_TOW_TILT_DEG
	int "Tow/jack tilt alert threshold (degrees, 0 = disabled)"
	default 6
	help
	  While asleep, the gravity vector is compared against a reference
	  snapped at sleep entry.  A sustained tilt beyond this angle raises a
	  tow/jack alert — catches slow, vibration-free lifts (flatbed ramps
	  reach 10-15°, jacking a corner 3-8°) that never trip the movement
	  wake.  Suspension settling is ~1-2°, so keep above ~4.

config APP_TOW_POLL_S
	int "Tow tilt poll interval during sleep (seconds)"
	default 30
	help
	  Sleep-loop wake cadence for the tilt check.  Each poll is a single
	  accelerometer read (~ms); the power cost is negligible on vehicle
	  power.

config APP_ACCEL_ALERT_PRIORITY
	int "Priority for accelerometer-derived alerts"
	default 2
	range -2 2
	help
	  Priority sent on the A,<prio>,<msg> line for every accel-derived
	  alert — movement, tow/jack tilt, parked impact and the awake impact
	  alert.  The server hands this straight to Pushover, whose scale is
	  -2 (log only, no notification), -1 (quiet, no sound), 0 (normal),
	  1 (high, bypasses quiet hours) and 2 (emergency: retries until
	  acknowledged, per the retry/expire settings in the server config).
	  Defaults to 2 — a tracker that only alerts on theft should insist.
	  Drop to 0 or -1 on a bench unit, or on a vehicle parked somewhere
	  that bumps it all day, so accel alerts still arrive and are logged
	  without demanding an acknowledgement.  Battery, self-test, FOTA and
	  command-reply alerts keep their own priorities.  Note the server
	  already demotes priority 2 to 0 for a device marked as garaged.

config APP_LED_ACCEL_WAKE
	bool "Blink the status LEDs on accelerometer wakes"
	default n
	help
	  When a sleep wake is qualified as movement/tow-tilt or as a parked
	  impact, play a pattern on LED1-3: a 1->2->3, hold, 3->2->1 sweep
	  (twice, 3.6 s) for movement or tilt, and a fast LED1+LED3 / LED2
	  alternation for an impact (5 s).  The pattern runs on a timer in
	  the background, so it carries on across the modem session that
	  sends the alert rather than delaying it.  Off by default —
	  a parked unit that blinks on every bump both wastes the vehicle
	  battery and advertises where it is.  Useful for install checks and
	  bench work.  Needs LED2/LED3 fitted to show the full pattern; with
	  only LED1 the patterns degrade to blinks on that one.

config APP_TOW_REARM_S
	int "Re-arm the tow/tilt alert after this long at a new resting attitude (seconds, 0 = never)"
	default 900
	help
	  A tow alert latches so one lift does not produce a stream of them,
	  and the latch only clears when the unit comes back within half the
	  threshold of the attitude snapped at sleep entry.  A vehicle set
	  down anywhere other than where it started therefore never re-arms,
	  and no later tilt can alert again for the rest of the parked
	  session.

	  Once the attitude has held still for this long, take it as the new
	  normal: re-snap the tilt reference, clear the latch, and alert
	  again only on a further tilt from there.  Stillness is required
	  precisely so this cannot re-arm mid-lift and hide the rest of a
	  slow tow.  Set 0 to keep the old behaviour.

config APP_PARKED_IMPACT_MG
	int "Parked impact alert threshold (milli-g)"
	default 800
	help
	  Peak | |a| - 1g | from the FIFO ring during an unconfirmed movement
	  wake (a "transient bump") that raises a parked-impact alert instead
	  of being ignored.  Sleep runs the accel at ±2 g, but each axis
	  clips independently, so the vector magnitude still reaches
	  2*sqrt(3) = 3.46 g and the deviation runs to ~2460 mg — bench hits
	  are logged at 2 g routinely.

